# Accepted exceptions for THIS repository. One regular expression per line, matched against
# "path:line".
#
# This is the PUBLIC repo, so the list stays as short as it can be: every line here is a
# place the scanner has been told to stop looking. Nothing goes in without a reason written
# beside it.

# KATOTTH codes are Ukraine's public register of administrative units - the identifier of a
# raion, not of a person or an account. The scanner cannot tell them apart from a tax or
# passport number by shape alone. Named file by file rather than opening all of web/, which
# is the part that actually gets published.
^web/raions\.geojson:
